asked whether the site describes the product the engineering documents
describe. Neither asked whether the backend is real, and nothing in
audit/scripts/ can see a database, an auth boundary or a telemetry
event.

The finding that sets the execution order: lib/types.ts:191-209 and
lib/validators.ts:447-462 accept fifteen telemetry event types;
migrations/001_initial_schema.sql:83-95 stores eleven. The four missing
are exactly the four the firmware contract owns, including the 1 Hz
pressure stream — the raw material for the closed-loop process
intelligence this company calls its moat. A device following the
contract is accepted by the validator and rejected by Postgres, which
surfaces as a 500 with no retry contract, no buffer and no dead-letter.

